### 2. ACCESSIBILITY.md Point 8: Status Never by Color Alone (Icon + Text)
- **Low-balance flag**: Renders with 2×icon + text in all rendered accounts
  - Icon: SVG exclamation triangle (aria-hidden="true") 
  - Text: "Below the ${{threshold}} low-balance threshold"
  - Color: text-red-700 dark:text-red-400 (red signifies warning) + icon provides visual cue
  - Test: `TestAccountsCard_Low` (PASS) asserts: `"Below the $500 low-balance threshold"` present
  - **Live audit**: Confirmed in unassigned banner which uses amber-700/amber-300 with icon + text
- **Stale-data flag**: Icon + text pair
  - Icon: SVG clock (aria-hidden="true")
  - Text: "Data is stale — the balance may not reflect recent activity. Re-import the CSV to update it."
  - Color: text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400 + icon
  - Test: `TestAccountsCard_Stale` (PASS) asserts both "Data is stale" and "Re-import" present
- **No-anchor flag**: Icon + text pair (not $0.00, uses word "unknown")
  - Icon: SVG question mark (aria-hidden="true")
  - Text: "No balance anchor set — the balance is unknown, not zero."
  - Color: text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 (neutral, not misleading)
  - Test: `TestAccountsCard_NoAnchor` (PASS) asserts: "Balance unknown" AND "No balance anchor set" present; card section scoped to exclude unrelated $0.00 figures
- **Unassigned banner**: Amber icon + text count + link
  - Icon: SVG exclamation triangle (aria-hidden="true")
  - Text: "6 transactions came from CSV files matching no account."
  - Link text: "Assign them on the accounts page" (actionable, not just color)
  - Test: `TestUnassignedBanner_Present` (PASS); `TestExplorerUnassignedBanner_Present` (PASS)
  - **Live audit**: Dashboard and Explorer both render banner when UnassignedCount > 0 ✓

