### 5. ACCESSIBILITY.md Point 13: Currency Sign Semantics (e.g., aria-label for negation)
- **Balance display**: Uses `formatMoney` filter which preserves sign in output (positive for balance shown, negative for withdrawal)
- **No-anchor state**: Uses word "Balance unknown" + link to /accounts page
  - NOT rendered as $0.00 (semantic difference: unknown ≠ zero balance)
  - Scoped test assertion ensures KPI $0 figures don't falsely trip the check
- **Projection amounts**: Uses `{{printf "%.0f" .Projection.X}}` to format thresholds/top-ups; prefix included in template text ("${{threshold}}" = sign + amount)
- **Test**: `TestAccountsCard_NoAnchor` (PASS) asserts card does NOT contain "$0.00" (critical ruling per GLOSSARY.md)

### 6. ACCESSIBILITY.md Point 14: Banners Dismissible & Not Re-announced Every Page Load
- **Unassigned banner**: Implemented with sessionStorage-scoped dismissal key
  - Key: `unassigned-banner-dismissed-{{.UnassignedCount}}` (scoped to current count)
  - On dismiss button click: stores key in sessionStorage, removes banner from DOM
  - On page load: checks sessionStorage; if key present, pre-removes banner before render
  - If count changes (e.g., new CSV uploaded), new count = new key = banner re-appears ✓
  - Template: `web/templates/components/unassigned_banner.html` lines 44–61
  - No aria-live re-announcement per page load; only on state change ✓
- **Test**: `TestUnassignedBanner_Present` (PASS) asserts sessionStorage integration; dismissal handled client-side ✓

